    <title>ConQEC: Concolic Testing for Quantum Error-Correcting Code Implementations</title>
    <link href="https://latifkedi.github.io/ahbar/?item=2026-10-25-33-conqec-concolic-testing-for-quantum"/>
    <link rel="related" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.31443v1"/>
    <id>https://latifkedi.github.io/ahbar/item/2026-10-25-33-conqec-concolic-testing-for-quantum</id>
    <updated>2026-10-22T15:40:04+00:00</updated>
    <summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;Quantum error-correcting code (QECC) implementations are hybrid software-control systems: measured syndromes drive decoder dispatch, recovery actions, and logical checks. Existing QECC verification techniques can prove formal obligations, and general quantum testing can expose final failures, but developers still lack a scalable testing workflow that generates concrete faults and explains where a QECC repair path first diverges. This paper presents ConQEC, to our knowledge the first concolic testing framework for QECC implementations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.31443v1&quot;&gt;arXiv CS (PL, SE, DB, DC, DS)&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;strong&gt;Tags:&lt;/strong&gt; #compilers #distributed-systems #quantum-computing #software-architecture&lt;/p&gt;</summary>
